knitted woollen caps. Each cap was individualized; the men recognized one another only by the pattern of stripes on the caps. The men were bundled up so tightly against the fierce cold that only their eyes were visible.</dc:description><dc:description xml:lang="nl">In 1980 onderzochten archeologen de graven van 185 Nederlandse mannen die in de 17de eeuw op of nabij
